t have enough to defend later.\n\nPassing and hoping my teammate saves us isn't a strategy because the Landlord can either play the card or force us to use our high card on the next round. My ♥2 is what's needed.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord has only 2 cards remaining, which is a critical "danger zone". If the Landlord holds a pair, passing now would allow him to play it and win the game immediately. As the player acting immediately after the Landlord ("Downstream Peasant"), it is my responsibility to block his high cards to prevent him from maintaining control. I have strong blocking cards (2 and Black Joker).\n\nReason: Playing the ♥2 is the best move. It successfully beats the Landlord\'s ♣K and forces him to either play the Red Joker (if he has it) or give up the lead. Using the 2 is more efficient than using the Black Joker, as it saves the highest card for a later critical moment while still effectively blocking the Landlord. Taking the lead will allow me to play a small single (like the 3) to force the Landlord to play his remaining cards one by one or break a potential pair.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥2"]}'}
